  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "sentence": "For weeks, our D.C. reporters chronicled a slow-motion political drama: Would Democrats and Republicans find a way to compromise before the government ran out of money?",
      "paragraph_id": 0,
      "word_count": 26,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 11.825,
      "duration": 11.825,
      "phoneme_count": 179
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "sentence": "Now that we know the answer, they\u2019re covering how the shutdown actually works.",
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "word_count": 13,
      "start_time": 11.825,
      "end_time": 17.05,
      "duration": 5.225,
      "phoneme_count": 72
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "sentence": "What happens when federal employees go home, and how might the shutdown end?",
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "word_count": 13,
      "start_time": 17.05,
      "end_time": 22.625,
      "duration": 5.575,
      "phoneme_count": 78
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "sentence": "For today\u2019s newsletter, I got answers from Carl Hulse, our chief Washington correspondent, and Eileen Sullivan, who covers the federal work force.",
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "word_count": 22,
      "start_time": 22.625,
      "end_time": 32.975,
      "duration": 10.35,
      "phoneme_count": 149
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "sentence": "What\u2019s at stake for both parties?",
      "paragraph_id": 2,
      "word_count": 6,
      "start_time": 32.975,
      "end_time": 35.525,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "phoneme_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "sentence": "Carl: Quite a bit.",
      "paragraph_id": 3,
      "word_count": 4,
      "start_time": 35.525,
      "end_time": 37.475,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "phoneme_count": 20
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "sentence": "Republicans want to show that they are able to wield their majority power and keep the government funded without giving in to what they see as unreasonable Democratic demands.",
      "paragraph_id": 3,
      "word_count": 29,
      "start_time": 37.475,
      "end_time": 49.325,
      "duration": 11.85,
      "phoneme_count": 175
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "sentence": "Democrats are trying to win health care concessions and also demonstrate that Republicans must treat them as legislative partners and not jam bills down their throats.",
      "paragraph_id": 3,
      "word_count": 26,
      "start_time": 49.325,
      "end_time": 60.875,
      "duration": 11.55,
      "phoneme_count": 171
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "sentence": "The outcome of the clash is likely to influence next year\u2019s midterm elections.",
      "paragraph_id": 3,
      "word_count": 13,
      "start_time": 60.875,
      "end_time": 66.6,
      "duration": 5.725,
      "phoneme_count": 79
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "sentence": "What are Democrats trying to get before they\u2019ll support the stopgap spending bill?",
      "paragraph_id": 4,
      "word_count": 13,
      "start_time": 66.6,
      "end_time": 71.825,
      "duration": 5.225,
      "phoneme_count": 80
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "sentence": "Carl: They want an extension of subsidies created during the pandemic for purchasing health coverage through the Affordable Care Act.",
      "paragraph_id": 5,
      "word_count": 20,
      "start_time": 71.825,
      "end_time": 80.65,
      "duration": 8.825,
      "phoneme_count": 130
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "sentence": "Otherwise, they say, premium costs will rise for millions of people.",
      "paragraph_id": 5,
      "word_count": 11,
      "start_time": 80.65,
      "end_time": 85.925,
      "duration": 5.275,
      "phoneme_count": 67
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "sentence": "Republicans say they are open to extending the subsidies, but only if the government reopens.",
      "paragraph_id": 5,
      "word_count": 15,
      "start_time": 85.925,
      "end_time": 92.6,
      "duration": 6.675,
      "phoneme_count": 95
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "sentence": "At least eight Democrats would need to join Republicans to pass a spending bill.",
      "paragraph_id": 5,
      "word_count": 14,
      "start_time": 92.6,
      "end_time": 98.075,
      "duration": 5.475,
      "phoneme_count": 80
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "sentence": "So far, three have.",
      "paragraph_id": 5,
      "word_count": 4,
      "start_time": 98.075,
      "end_time": 100.25,
      "duration": 2.175,
      "phoneme_count": 20
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "sentence": "Some federal employees are \u201cexcepted\u201d from the shutdown and have to work.",
      "paragraph_id": 6,
      "word_count": 12,
      "start_time": 100.25,
      "end_time": 105.525,
      "duration": 5.275,
      "phoneme_count": 74
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "sentence": "Who qualifies?",
      "paragraph_id": 6,
      "word_count": 2,
      "start_time": 105.525,
      "end_time": 107.4,
      "duration": 1.875,
      "phoneme_count": 15
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "sentence": "Eileen: Each department identifies people critical to protecting life and property, and they keep working during a government shutdown.",
      "paragraph_id": 7,
      "word_count": 19,
      "start_time": 107.4,
      "end_time": 116.575,
      "duration": 9.175,
      "phoneme_count": 136
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "sentence": "Think federal law enforcement officers, air traffic controllers and T.S.A. officers at airports.",
      "paragraph_id": 7,
      "word_count": 13,
      "start_time": 116.575,
      "end_time": 123.875,
      "duration": 7.3,
      "phoneme_count": 100
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "sentence": "Not all agencies rely on appropriations for funding.",
      "paragraph_id": 8,
      "word_count": 8,
      "start_time": 123.875,
      "end_time": 128.4,
      "duration": 4.525,
      "phoneme_count": 55
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "sentence": "That is why some government services continue uninterrupted.",
      "paragraph_id": 8,
      "word_count": 8,
      "start_time": 128.4,
      "end_time": 133.35,
      "duration": 4.95,
      "phoneme_count": 65
    },
    {
